# Responsibility: Keep the build context to what an image needs - no secrets, no history, no local trees.
# Boundaries: it shapes what Docker can see; the Dockerfile's COPY lines decide what is actually copied.

# Secrets and credentials. COPY is already narrow, but a future `COPY . .` must not be able to ship
# these. Root-anchored, so it is THE directory that is excluded rather than any path ending in the
# same word.
.env
*.pem
*.key
/secrets/
/.local/

# Repository metadata. History is not a build input, and shipping it would put every past value of
# every file - including ones since removed - inside the image.
.git/

# Repository-local scratch, evidence and redirected tool caches. 112M, none of it a build input.
/BETA/

# Heavy local trees the image never needs: the 1.7G virtualenv, and the runtime roots the
# application writes at their configured defaults.
/.venv/
/data/
/workspaces/
/deploy/output/

# Packaging output. The wheel the image installs is built inside the build, never uploaded into it.
/build/
/dist/
*.egg-info/

# Python bytecode - never bundle a host's compiled cache into an image.
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Tests run from the repo (unit) or a bind mount (integration), never baked in.
tests/

# Node workspace artefacts (the console build). The console stage COPYs apps/console/ AFTER its
# own `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, so an unignored host node_modules - a pnpm symlink farm
# that does not resolve the same way inside the image - would land on top of that freshly
# filtered install, and a stale .next would ride along with it. Measured on a developer machine:
# apps/console/.next ~99M, root node_modules ~467M. Invisible on a fresh CI checkout, poisonous
# locally. **/ so every workspace (root, apps/*, packages/*) is covered, not just the console's.
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/.turbo/
